{"id": 29, "ts": 1782986518.8980613, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_3", "message": "I appreciate the detailed concerns raised about B\u2019s weak memory for numbers and the communication style issues of both B and C. Given that accurate numerical handling is non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul operations, B\u2019s attention\u2011and\u2011information\u2011accuracy deficit is a critical safety risk that is hard to remediate. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, while egocentric and less eager to pursue further education, is described as 100\u202f% reliable, makes correct decisions quickly, and fosters a positive crew atmosphere\u2014attributes that directly support decision quality, stress resilience, and crew cooperation. The new information that Candidate\u202fD solves problems extremely well, demonstrates strong technical competence, and handles unexpected events adequately adds a compelling profile, though we still lack evidence on his crew\u2011cooperation. Considering the current evidence, I am less convinced that B can outweigh the memory issue, and I therefore shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**, while noting that D may become a contender pending further insight into his teamwork behavior."}
